### Lasius Hexapod REST Control API
### PyCharm / IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client Specification

@base = http://192.168.0.123:8000
@leg = left_rear
@order_id = ord_sample_01


### Status & Hardware Telemetry

### 1. Robot Operational Status & Active Control State
GET {{base}}/api/v1/status

### 2. Raspberry Pi System & Hardware KPIs (CPU, RAM, Temp, Power Health, Wi-Fi)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/system/stats

### 3. Physical Robot Geometry & Kinematic Layout
GET {{base}}/api/v1/robot



### Orders & Motion Arbitration

### 4. List Recent Order History
GET {{base}}/api/v1/orders

### 5. Submit New Locomotion Order (Walk Forward)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "set_walk",
  "params": {
    "x": 0.0,
    "y": 1.0,
    "z": 0.0
  },
  "priority": 10,
  "source": "http_client"
}

### 6. Submit Gait Pattern Change Order (Tripod / Wave / Ripple)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "set_gait_type",
  "params": {
    "gait": "tripod"
  },
  "priority": 10,
  "source": "http_client"
}

### 7. Query Specific Order by ID
GET {{base}}/api/v1/orders/{{order_id}}


### Leg Diagnostics & Motion Tests

### 8. Run Harmonic Step Cycle Test on Target Leg
POST {{base}}/api/v1/legs/{{leg}}/test
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cycles": 3,
  "stride": 36.0,
  "lift": 30.0
}

### 9. Move Target Leg to Neutral Stance Position
POST {{base}}/api/v1/legs/{{leg}}/stance
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hold": 0.0
}


### Hardware Safety & Server Daemon Lifecycle

### 10. Immediate Emergency Stop (Halts Motion, Relaxes PWM)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/emergency_stop

### 11. Relax All 18 Servos (Disable PWM Outputs)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/relax

### 12. Restart Lasius Server Daemon (Halts Servos & Re-executes Process)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/server/restart
Content-Type: application/json

{}



### OpenAPI 3.1 Specification Endpoints


### 13. Download OpenAPI 3.1 Spec (YAML)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/openapi.yaml

### 14. Retrieve OpenAPI 3.1 Spec (JSON)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/openapi.json
